{"base":{"art_sha256":"0ece61b53654a0192d72ee642342bfa6dd92e94526a406c0d54eb9545155ad2a","exporter_sha256":"a59ea668fa5f46111044ac00e4702c8037560a2fb4f97ac57761ee5abcc05261","world_sha256":"9e179490cafeebffc47bfc5af7aeb5e714c0a51931dc86e7e2cc38ce811ee74b"},"brief":"plaza-night","candidate":"D","format":"VERDANDI-INTENT","layout":[],"prompt":"make the cantilevers more imposing","rationale":"The owner's note on the round's sheet: 'Make the nearest cantilever lower and larger in frame, then keep its underside mostly dark with a narrow row of warm fixtures along the edge.' The north slab alone, brought down from 7.0 to 4.6 m and made 2.2 m deep, over the same two rows of cells (a third row would put the plaza's pole lamps under it, lighting the underside); dark beneath but for a row of small warm fixtures, one a metre, along the edge that faces the plaza. The other slabs, the lamps and the neon as they are.","revision":["= canopy plaza concrete_slab 4.6 19,10 28,11 deep 2.2 edgelit 255,178,112 120"],"scope":["plaza/canopy/*"],"version":"0"}